{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019sfCkNt2r7e7PZyCsZPEsR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MtDGfJB4TAF8jvCqQ5LX65","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/petardjukic/2025-objectives/go-unix-utils/.cobbler/measure-20260224-215150.yaml","content":"- index: 0\n  title: \"pkg/testutils: Implement DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests harness (prd001 R1-R5)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd001-testutils.yaml (full PRD for the differential testing harness)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (component description for pkg/testutils, project structure, design decisions)\n      - go.mod (module path: github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: create\n        note: DiffTest struct, Normalize type, RunDiffTests function, comparison and reporting logic\n      - path: pkg/testutils/normalize.go\n        action: create\n        note: TimestampNormalizer, ComposeNormalizers helper\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Tests for RunDiffTests, TimestampNormalizer, file-state comparison, timeout behavior\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Define a DiffTest struct with fields: Name (string for subtest naming), Args ([]string), Stdin ([]byte, nil means no stdin/EOF immediately), Env ([]string, nil means inherit test process environment), ExitCode (int), Normalize ([]func([]byte) []byte, nil or empty means no normalization), WorkDir (string, empty means create a per-test temp directory), and ExpectedFiles (map[string][]byte for file-state comparison, nil means no file comparison). Define a Normalize function type as func([]byte) []byte. Traces prd001-testutils R1.1-R1.4, R5.1.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary string, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest) that iterates over the test slice, runs each as a named subtest via t.Run(test.Name, ...), executes both binaries with identical args, stdin, and environment, and compares their outputs. Each subtest is independent. Traces prd001-testutils R2.1, R3.6, AC1.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement binary execution using os/exec.CommandContext with context.WithTimeout. Default timeout is 10 seconds. Capture stdout and stderr into bytes.Buffer and exit code from exec.ExitError.ExitCode(). When WorkDir is empty, create a per-test temp directory via t.TempDir() and set both binaries' working directory to it. Produce no output to the test process stdout or stderr during a passing test. Traces prd001-testutils R2.1-R2.5.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement comparison logic: apply each function in the DiffTest.Normalize slice in order to both binaries' stdout and stderr before comparison. Compare normalized stdout byte-for-byte, normalized stderr byte-for-byte, and exit codes exactly. On any divergence, report: the DiffTest args, stdin content (truncated to 256 bytes if longer), reference binary stdout, Go binary stdout, reference stderr, Go stderr, and both exit codes via t.Errorf. Traces prd001-testutils R3.1-R3.5.\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Implement a TimestampNormalizer (func([]byte) []byte) that replaces common strftime timestamp patterns with the fixed placeholder string 'TIMESTAMP'. Must match the default ts format '%b %d %H:%M:%S' (e.g., 'Feb 19 12:34:56') and bare 'HH:MM:SS' elapsed-time format (e.g., '00:00:05'). Implement ComposeNormalizers(fns ...func([]byte) []byte) func([]byte) []byte that returns a single normalizer applying each function in order. Traces prd001-testutils R4.1-R4.3.\"\n      - id: R6\n        text: \"Implement file-state comparison: when DiffTest.ExpectedFiles is non-nil, after both binaries exit, for each key (file path relative to WorkDir) in ExpectedFiles, read the file written by each binary and compare content byte-for-byte. Report divergence in the same format as stdout divergence (file path, expected content, actual content). Traces prd001-testutils R5.1-R5.2.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Primary source file is difftest.go (named after the primary exported type DiffTest), not testutils.go. Package name is testutils under pkg/testutils/. This follows the project convention that Go packages name the primary source file after the primary exported type.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use os/exec.CommandContext with context.WithTimeout for binary execution. Default timeout is 10 seconds per prd001-testutils R2.3. Extract exit code via exec.ExitError; when the error is a context.DeadlineExceeded, report a timeout failure with the binary path and timeout duration.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Normalize is stored as a slice of func([]byte) []byte on DiffTest, applied in order per prd001-testutils R4.3. When the slice is nil or empty, no normalization is applied. ComposeNormalizers is a convenience for callers that prefer a single function.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"TimestampNormalizer uses regexp.ReplaceAll to match patterns. The month-day-time pattern matches three-letter month abbreviation, one or two digit day, and HH:MM:SS. The elapsed pattern matches standalone HH:MM:SS at line start. Both are replaced with the literal string 'TIMESTAMP'.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"A Go test file can define a []DiffTest slice and call RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests) from a TestXxx function with no other setup beyond building the binaries.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"A passing test run produces no output on the test process stdout or stderr. A failing test prints the triggering args, stdin (truncated to 256 bytes), and both binaries' stdout, stderr, and exit code.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"TimestampNormalizer replaces a string like 'Feb 19 12:34:56' with 'TIMESTAMP' and replaces a string like '00:00:05' at line start with 'TIMESTAMP'.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"A DiffTest with ExpectedFiles set correctly reports failure when the Go binary writes different file content than the reference binary.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"A DiffTest where a binary exceeds the 10-second timeout fails with a message containing 'timeout' rather than hanging the test run.\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"All pkg/testutils code compiles with go build ./pkg/testutils/... and passes go vet ./pkg/testutils/... with no errors. All tests pass with go test ./pkg/testutils/...\"\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":71741,"cache_read_input_tokens":15594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":71741},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6462fec0-efde-4cfe-9af1-9de8cea35db6","uuid":"05c8a4e9-289a-43f6-a6dd-0b422e1cf600"}
